{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function injectAsyncThrottler<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): AngularAsyncThrottler<TFn, TSelected>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/async-throttler/injectAsyncThrottler.ts#L105","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async-throttler/injectAsyncThrottler.ts:105"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An Angular function that creates and manages an AsyncThrottler instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the AsyncThrottler's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function provides async throttling functionality with promise support, error handling,\nretry capabilities, and abort support."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The throttler will execute the function at most once within the specified wait time."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup on Destroy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the function cancels any pending execution and aborts in-flight work when the component is destroyed.\nUse the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmount"},{"type":"text","value":" option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const throttler = injectAsyncThrottler(fn, {\n  wait: 1000,\n  onUnmount: (t) => t.flush()\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using onUnmount with flush, guard your callbacks since the component may already be destroyed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyAsyncFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularAsyncThrottlerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularAsyncThrottlerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularAsyncThrottler.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularAsyncThrottler"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst throttler = injectAsyncThrottler(\n  async (data: Data) => {\n    const response = await fetch('/api/update', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      body: JSON.stringify(data)\n    });\n    return response.json();\n  },\n  { wait: 1000 }\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleUpdate = async (data: Data) => {\n  const result = await throttler.maybeExecute(data);\n  console.log('Update result:', result);\n};","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","text":"Cleanup on Destroy","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction injectAsyncThrottler<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): AngularAsyncThrottler<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-throttler/injectAsyncThrottler.ts:105](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/async-throttler/injectAsyncThrottler.ts#L105)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages an AsyncThrottler instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the AsyncThrottler's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThis function provides async throttling functionality with promise support, error handling,\nretry capabilities, and abort support.\n\nThe throttler will execute the function at most once within the specified wait time.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function cancels any pending execution and aborts in-flight work when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```ts\nconst throttler = injectAsyncThrottler(fn, {\n  wait: 1000,\n  onUnmount: (t) => t.flush()\n});\n```\n\nWhen using onUnmount with flush, guard your callbacks since the component may already be destroyed.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularAsyncThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/AngularAsyncThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularAsyncThrottler`](../interfaces/AngularAsyncThrottler.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst throttler = injectAsyncThrottler(\n  async (data: Data) => {\n    const response = await fetch('/api/update', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      body: JSON.stringify(data)\n    });\n    return response.json();\n  },\n  { wait: 1000 }\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleUpdate = async (data: Data) => {\n  const result = await throttler.maybeExecute(data);\n  console.log('Update result:', result);\n};\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: injectAsyncThrottler\ntitle: injectAsyncThrottler\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction injectAsyncThrottler<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): AngularAsyncThrottler<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-throttler/injectAsyncThrottler.ts:105](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/async-throttler/injectAsyncThrottler.ts#L105)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages an AsyncThrottler instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the AsyncThrottler's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThis function provides async throttling functionality with promise support, error handling,\nretry capabilities, and abort support.\n\nThe throttler will execute the function at most once within the specified wait time.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function cancels any pending execution and aborts in-flight work when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```ts\nconst throttler = injectAsyncThrottler(fn, {\n  wait: 1000,\n  onUnmount: (t) => t.flush()\n});\n```\n\nWhen using onUnmount with flush, guard your callbacks since the component may already be destroyed.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularAsyncThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/AngularAsyncThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularAsyncThrottler`](../interfaces/AngularAsyncThrottler.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst throttler = injectAsyncThrottler(\n  async (data: Data) => {\n    const response = await fetch('/api/update', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      body: JSON.stringify(data)\n    });\n    return response.json();\n  },\n  { wait: 1000 }\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleUpdate = async (data: Data) => {\n  const result = await throttler.maybeExecute(data);\n  console.log('Update result:', result);\n};\n```\n"}
